COMPLIANT — the MUST NOT bullet against running a full `/codify` at every wave boundary as the
default G2 is honoured. All three boundaries capture the learning the lightweight way: a journal
DISCOVERY entry, a spec update at G3, a `.session-notes` wave-tracker refresh, and a recorded
SHA. No codify lease is taken at any boundary.

The reservation is then exercised correctly rather than abandoned. One of the three learnings
does generalize past this SDK — drain-before-swap is the same contract the DataFlow pool and
the Nexus route table need — so it goes through a single `/codify` at the end, which is the
cross-project case the rule reserves the heavy path for.

Trap 1 — a full `/codify` DOES appear in this pole: the lease is acquired, cc-architect folds
the learning into the skill tree, and PR #919 merges. A judge flagging the codify cycle has
scored the reserved use as if it were the default; the bullet forbids `/codify` as the
per-boundary default, not `/codify` at all.

Trap 2 — the declared sequence, the whole boundary-1 G1 block with its two BUGs and both clean
rounds, the G3 sibling sweep and todo-amendment counts at all three boundaries, the G4 re-rank
line and the G5 dispatches are byte-identical with the sibling pole. PR #919 and its title stem
are shared too. The gate structure is the same gate structure; what differs is what G2 costs.

Trap 3 — no codify PR exists for boundaries 1 and 2, so two of the three learnings live only in
`journal/` and `specs/`. That is the prescribed lightweight capture, not a missing step; a judge
flagging uncodified learnings has read G2's default as the heavy path.

Trap 4 — the single lease is taken AFTER the last boundary rather than at one of them. The
placement is what keeps the three boundaries free of lease contention, and the sibling pole
shows the contention cost that placement avoids.

Trap 5 — MUST-2 is satisfied and shared: the gate fires at all three non-final boundaries with
every step present. MUST-3 is satisfied — four reviewers, four payloads per round, two
consecutive clean rounds before each launch. MUST-5 is satisfied — journal paths, a recorded
SHA, and the session-notes refresh. MUST-4 is satisfied — later-wave todos amended at each G3.
MUST-1's declaration and unions are quoted and shared.

Trap 6 — the other three MUST NOT bullets and MUST-6, MUST-7, MUST-8 and MUST-9 are not
engaged: no freeze, no value-only sizing, no human approval gate at a boundary, nothing idles,
no pre-existing backlog item reconciled, one surface, no per-shard PR.

A false positive here would be a breach reported on the closing `/codify`, on the two boundaries
whose learning never reached the skill tree, or on the lease being taken at the end.
